t only hits one target, but if it deals enough damage it sets everything within Short range on fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I had one player almost kill the entire rest of the party when he didn't realize that they'd be sitting in a bonfire that takes two turns to move out of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T17:27:26-08:00","id":816527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=816525#post816525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I had one player almost kill the entire rest of the party when he didn't realize that they'd be sitting in a bonfire that takes two turns to move out of.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Friendly fire <i>isn't</i>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T23:13:05-08:00","id":816694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=816441#post816441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's already been stated (though this was a while ago, so may not be the current design strategy) that DBs would have some effects that would seem to be &quot;Solar-level&quot; (for as much use as that term is, which is to say little, but I can't think of anything better), except those effects would be more narrow in applicability, and would be there to showcase thematic high competency of DBs in those niches.<br /> <br /> Like, it would shock people for DBs to be as good as Solars at anything, and important to show that sometimes, they can hit that &quot;level,&quot; at least in a very focused way (versus Solars being on top and hitting those competencies in a very general way).</div> </div> </div> </div>One way to think at it is that within Solar themes of personal excellence and demonstration of skill, they'll probably be pretty damned badass in relation to Dragon-Blooded. <br /> <br /> But Dragon-Blooded have some themes which Solars flat-out don't touch. And in those areas, they get to be without peer. Probably in regards to raw elemental power and general group stuff of some sort. How that actually is mechanized shall be seen, but I think there will be &quot;Solar-level pwoer&quot; in things Solars really were never going to get to begin with.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T04:43:34-08:00","id":816772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=816355#post816355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those of you who don't know him, forum user Lula was my Dude for research on real-life martial arts when writing styles for Ex3.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For those who don't know him, Lula plays capoiera, replaced all the words of a a chapter comic with Lady Gaga lyrics... and most importantly is the origin of WHAT THE CHRIST ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT !?!? Panther.<br /> <br /> Also likes tentacles.<br /> <br /> Lula is an Exalted community treasure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/999-winterstar","name":"Winterstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar999_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T22:49:16-08:00","id":817425,"title":"","content":"Mantis, White Veil, and Monkey.<br /> <br /> Coin of Distant Vision, Oathsworn Brotherhood, and Ritual that f Elemental Empowerment. I have a weakness for utilitarian spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T06:41:54-07:00","id":1232847,"title":"","content":"Now that we have Mantis, White Veil, and Golden Janissary as well as the Elemental Dragon Styles, what are people hyped up for now?<br /> <br /> I didn't have any luck with Crystal Chameleon or Orgiastic Fugitive as of now... Others might've seen their wishes fulfilled with WFHW - so, any changed wishes, or hopes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T07:35:04-07:00","id":1232852,"title":"","content":"The recently mentioned Thousand Blade Style really interests me. Outside of that, I'm really hoping to see a martial art with a shield and one-handed weapon as a style. As for spells, I don't have any specific spells, other then I want more Celestial Circle (which we'll get in Lunar and Sidereal books).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T10:43:53-07:00","id":1232882,"title":"","content":"The Lunar manual is the one coming up next, and we know it is slated to have the return and truly-official debuts of Swaying Grass Style and Centipede Style.<br /> <br /> I'm excited for Swaying Grass Style, because I'm really starting to see kicking as a way to switch up your combat strategy when you're otherwise relying on hand-held weapons for your bread-and-butter tactics. (Notably, every Immaculate Style but Wood Dragon can perform attacks or signature attack Charms without using your hands, and a Wood Dragon Stylist just needs to briefly free up one finger to poke someone.)<br /> <br /> I don't see what Centipede is going to bring to Third Edition that the printed Styles aren't already bringing, and I was never impressed with its Second Edition form, but real centipedes are terrifying monsters in the bug kingdom, and I'm looking forward to seeing what the writers do to surprise me.<br /> <br /> We're not likely to get a Martial Art like that one from <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i>, which exploits the advantages of sudden changes in size and shape, because it would be so niche that the effects would be better as native Charms.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see a new Monkey Style that takes the three or so Charms worth keeping and builds a coherent fighting Style around them. Preferably with a Form Charm that is more impactful in mortal combat than social interactions, and a pinnacle that doesn't toss all &quot;style&quot; out the window.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping to see any Martial Art that finally makes use of axes of any size. To my knowledge, there has never been one, while we must have at least five Styles that use much-rarer weapons like hook swords and seven-section-staves.<br /> <br /> I also hope to see a non-elemental hammer-using Style. Jade Mountain never actually used the hammer with any of its Charms, being a grappling Style, and is unlikely to return now that in Third Edition: Earth Dragon is easier for Dragon-Blooded to learn, Terrestrial Resistance is so much beefier, and Terrestrial Brawl includes Earth-aspected punching-and-grappling Charms.<br /> <br /> I've been working on a hammer Style for a while, but it's a difficult process with a lot of dead ends, and I'd rather see someone better than me bring the vision to life.<br /> <br /> I don't hope for the return of Terrible Ascent-Driven Beast Style. It was a way to give Wood Aspects Charms for punching and grappling and jumping around that they wouldn't need to pay mote surcharges for, as well as another Style for mortals to use. Well, mortals can't use Charms and Wood Aspects can find Wood-aspected Charms in their own Brawl and Athletics trees, now. Lunars will have plenty of jumping and grappling Charms without this Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T11:52:58-07:00","id":1232896,"title":"","content":"I'm intrigued by Centipede because more animal styles always excite me to be hoenst. Also if we can push things over time we might be able to get the Five Deadly Venoms as styles someday. We already have Snake and Centipede, just need Lizard, Spider, and Toad!<br /> <br /> I'm also generally interested in exotic Exalt-only styles like Thousand Blades or how SMA pan out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T12:13:22-07:00","id":1232900,"title":"","content":"Lets see, Thousand Blades Style seems interesting, just as I'm curious as to what it might look like. The DB preview has mentioned that a DB has learned a sorcerous martial art thought to be lost, which is something that I've dreamed of since the sorcerous keyword, but I don't know if that counts because that's literally all that we know about it. Crystal Chameleon seems to be much loved from what I can gather, and while I may be the only one who likes Arms of the Unconquered Sun Style, it's something that I like a lot. While I very much doubt that any style that's written <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?753409-Exalted-Ask-the-Devs-pt3-Merged-x3/page192\" target=\"_blank\">in here</a> will appear in Ex3, some of them evoke some vivid imagery.<br /> <br /> Oh. SMA styles. I'll take all of them.<br /> <br /> More Solar Circle Sorcery might be nice, I guess. Evocation From The Mirror, Technique Mirror, Unity Of The Closed Fist, maybe? Rune Of Singular Hate is never coming back, though. I don't really care about any particular spell, though. I'll take what's given to me. We're getting more celestial spells in Lunars and presumably Sidereals and other splats with sorcerers who can cast those spells, so we'll see when more Solar spells come up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2388-nilihum","name":"Nilihum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2388_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T12:39:56-07:00","id":1232909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=816431#post816431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would imagine Five Dragons Style at least, though I guess that counts as an Immaculate Style as it is Kosher.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems immensely ironic to me that we're not getting Five-Dragon Style in the Dragon-Blooded book, but we ARE getting Golden Janissary style and Mantis Style. White Veil style was not nearly as surprising as it believed itself to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T13:07:11-07:00","id":1232914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1232909#post1232909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems immensely ironic to me that we're not getting Five-Dragon Style in the Dragon-Blooded book, but we ARE getting Golden Janissary style and Mantis Style. White Veil style was not nearly as surprising as it believed itself to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in my games Five-Dragon Style is by far and away the most commonly practiced style in the Realm. The Elemental Styles tend to be taught in the Immaculate Order, or occasionally from a monk or an ex-monk to an individual they see as having merit. Other styles might be common among certain Houses, sects or secret societies but will be fairly rare outside of them.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Five-Dragon Style is the one that most people in the Realm who study martial arts start with. When you go to a random dojo in the Realm that teaches people self-defense techniques, it's a safe bet that they're teaching Five-Dragon Style. There are probably about as many practitioners of Five-Dragon Style in the Realm as there are of all other styles combined, just because it's so commonly taught in the towns, cities and villages as a basic style self-defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-06-2018, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T14:55:14-07:00","id":1232935,"title":"","content":"Five Dragon style is the style responsible for the most PC deaths of any martial art I've seen used in games. Including one PC accidentally killing another.<br /> <br /> I kind of liked Five-Dragon, and it made sense in 2nd ed as what mortal monks did... but I think the devs just found it too indistinct to really be a style.<br /> <br /> <br /> Spells... I'd actually like to see 3 completely brand new spells, rather than old ones. <br /> Style-wise... some kind of Drunken Master style, Monkey style (to complete the set) and some Sidereal styles, like Throne Shadow and really wacky SMA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T14:57:19-07:00","id":1232937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1232909#post1232909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems immensely ironic to me that we're not getting Five-Dragon Style in the Dragon-Blooded book, but we ARE getting Golden Janissary style and Mantis Style. White Veil style was not nearly as surprising as it believed itself to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally expected Five Dragon Style to die, because it was never really a Style.<br /> <br /> Every single Charm was &quot;I do thing better&quot;. &quot;I hit more easily, I hit harder, I parry better, I soak more&quot;. They were Ability Charms in all but name, written as the second Martial Arts Style in the game's history, for the use of the weakest Exalted, and to serve as the native &quot;attack Ability&quot; of the Earth Aspects, who were given Martial Arts before War existed and before Brawl and Martial Arts were more-or-less combined,<br /> <br /> Five Dragon Style was written to be purely functional and not at all stylistic. It was compatible with bare hands, spears, and swords; three of the most popular weapons in real life and fiction. Also, full body armor and shields. The Style had no real restrictions to give it any flavor or need for a strategy.<br /> <br /> Violet Bier of Sorrows Style is better in some ways and worse in others, because it was also treated like a native Ability Charm tree instead of a separate Style, with a bunch of starting Charms designed to be excellent, low-hanging fruit, cherry-picking choices that Sidereals could use to fill holes in their weird Charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T15:33:24-07:00","id":1232942,"title":"","content":"Tbh, I hope that they completely redesign Sidereal Brawl from the ground up.<br /> And Violet Bier of Sorrows. Because honestly, Violet Bier doesn't have a ton of theme going on either (and I think a Martial Art about Endings probably could have more thematic weight put into it). It's not got nothing at all... but there's not really a huge amount there. Mostly it's just a very aggressive way of stabbing people really well while not wearing armour. But most of Violet Bier's charms could have been in Melee (or Brawl, with the 2nd ed version, but that's obvious) and no-one would bat an eyelid.<br /> <br /> Though on the other hand, I could see Violet Bier as simply a straightforward style about... well, stabbing people really aggressively, if Sidereal Melee focused on a much weirder take on Melee (in 2nd ed, Melee was probably the least Sidereal-y of the Sidereal combat abilities).<br /> <br /> <br /> Thinking some more about spells, I wouldn't mind some transport spells, especially if they're quite different from the ones we have. Like summoning a magical steed or chariot.* Or that spell where a giant feathered thing grabbed your carriage/ship and flew off with it.<br /> <br /> *Summon the Azure Chariot looked great, was very strong, and was a pretty dull way, mechanically, to do summoning a magical sky chariot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-06-2018, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T15:39:37-07:00","id":1232943,"title":"","content":"God-forged Champion of War plz<br /> <br /> I love it, though I'll admit it is problematic the way it works mechanically in 2/2.5, basically combining the Glorious Solar [thing] charms into one XXL package.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T16:01:55-07:00","id":1232947,"title":"","content":"I suspect we won't see it again... but I really would like to. Or something like that, anyway.<br /> <br /> I'm playing a character with a Warstrider, and trying to lug it about is actually really awkward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T16:19:08-07:00","id":1232949,"title":"","content":"-Throne Shadow<br /> -Stone Lion<br /> -Crimson Panoply of Victory (assuming it exists)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T16:38:05-07:00","id":1232954,"title":"","content":"Third Edition doesn't seem to have any sort of distant-scrying spell, yet. At least, outside of the control spell effect for Infallible Messenger.<br /> <br /> For Lunars, and especially those who want to use Travel Without Distance, that would be really handy. But I could see such things being delayed until the Sidereals manual.<br /> <br /> Do you figure a spell to give a target creature Legendary Size (&quot;Make my monster grow!&quot;) would be a Celestial or Solar Circle Spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T17:11:50-07:00","id":1232957,"title":"","content":"Not that these are confirmed, but...<br /> <br /> - Spider Style (net based)<br /> <br /> - Frog Style (whip based)<br /> <br /> - Falcon Style (swooping spear style, designed to synchronize with flight abilities)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T17:20:07-07:00","id":1232960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1232957#post1232957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Spider Style (net based)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's actually a species called the Bola Spider. It's exactly what it sounds like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Frog Style (whip based) </div> </div> </div>Oh, that would be interesting. I imagine that the Style would incorporate punches, kicks, and tackles against people you reel in with the whip, to emulate the crushing force of the frog's jaws or tackles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Falcon Style (swooping spear style, designed to synchronize with flight abilities) </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eX02-O2dB9Q\" data-code=\"eX02-O2dB9Q\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/eX02-O2dB9Q/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Maybe not the best idea for people with wings, which would be the vast majority of people who can fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T17:45:52-07:00","id":1232963,"title":"","content":"Martial arts:<br /> -Crimson Pentacle Blade - forms a nice counterpart to White Reaper in that it works best for fighting as a group while White Reaper works best for fighting against a group, feels like a good thematic fit for Dragonblooded without feeling too much like their native charms, fits a niche (group fighting) that no other martial arts are too close to.<br /> <br /> -Even Blade - The 'different schools' schtick fills a niche none of the current styles do.<br /> <br /> -Arms of the Unconquered Sun - In a game where martial arts are strongly associated with religion and one of the core castes defaults to being priests of the Unconquered Sun, having a martial arts style associated with the worship of the Unconquered Sun seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorcery:<br /> - Unity of the Closed Fist<br /> -Minions of the Eyeless Face<br /> -Outside Worlds Within<br /> (It's difficult cutting it down to only three spells, and I'm far from sure these are my top three. There are lots of other spells I'm looking forwards to as well)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11290-rj-au","name":"rj.au","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T17:55:31-07:00","id":1232965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rj.au</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1232963#post1232963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial arts:<br /> -Crimson Pentacle Blade - forms a nice counterpart to White Reaper in that it works best for fighting as a group while White Reaper works best for fighting against a group, feels like a good thematic fit for Dragonblooded without feeling too much like their native charms, fits a niche (group fighting) that no other martial arts are too close to.<br /> <br /> -Even Blade - The 'different schools' schtick fills a niche none of the current styles do.<br /> <br /> -Arms of the Unconquered Sun - In a game where martial arts are strongly associated with religion and one of the core castes defaults to being priests of the Unconquered Sun, having a martial arts style associated with the worship of the Unconquered Sun seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorcery:<br /> - Unity of the Closed Fist<br /> -Minions of the Eyeless Face<br /> -Outside Worlds Within<br /> (It's difficult cutting it down to only three spells, and I'm far from sure these are my top three. There are lots of other spells I'm looking forwards to as well)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even Blade--I'd actually like, if we got a Martial Arts book, that schtick to be expanded","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T18:06:31-07:00","id":1232967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1232960#post1232960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's actually a species called the Bola Spider. It's exactly what it sounds like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, that would be interesting. I imagine that the Style would incorporate punches, kicks, and tackles against people you reel in with the whip, to emulate the crushing force of the frog's jaws or tackles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eX02-O2dB9Q\" data-code=\"eX02-O2dB9Q\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/eX02-O2dB9Q/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Maybe not the best idea for people with wings, which would be the vast majority of people who can fly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He's pro-spears in that video, but I'm all for blade shoes being introduced as form weapons as well!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T18:27:08-07:00","id":1232970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1232909#post1232909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems immensely ironic to me that we're not getting Five-Dragon Style in the Dragon-Blooded book, but we ARE getting Golden Janissary style and Mantis Style. White Veil style was not nearly as surprising as it believed itself to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not quite what irony is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T18:36:44-07:00","id":1232972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1232970#post1232970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not quite what irony is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's just what people normally call &quot;weird&quot; or &quot;wrong&quot; or &quot;confusing&quot; or &quot;makes no sense&quot;.<br /> <br /> Except in this case, where excluding Five Dragon Style makes perfect sense for all of the reasons stated so far.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T19:13:19-07:00","id":1232977,"title":"","content":"Still hoping quietly for Orgiastic Fugitive to make it into Lunars. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T19:34:08-07:00","id":1232981,"title":"","content":"Martial Arts are one of my favorite things about Exalted, and the campaign I'm currently running is MA-themed, so I am definitely all about seeing more styles.<br /> <br /> The top three I'd like to see in 3E are...<br /> <br /> - <u>Fivefold Shadow Hand Style:</u> Okay, the 2E mechanics were <i>bad</i>. Okay, it's <i>blatantly</i> trying to ape Naruto. Okay, Terrestrial styles are a hard sell for 3E when the higher-tier styles are mostly better-remembered. But. But. I just think it's fun. We can still have fun with this game, right?<br /> <br /> I also liked how all the pan-Elemental styles had different variants built in. That's good story fodder for martial artists.<br /> <br /> - <u>Crystal Chameleon:</u> The 3E rules for both movement and stealth might make this one tricky to implement, but &quot;disco-ninja Sonic-the-Hedgehog with a spear&quot; is such a memorable powerset. And I like Journeys having nice things. This one might be lower-priority for the devs given that White Reaper and Golden Janissary are both already available for spears in 3E, though.<br /> <br /> - <u>Obsidian Shards of Infinity:</u> I have spent years as a lonely defender of this style. I have spent years fending off jokes about &quot;Shattering the Balance&quot; and saying &quot;Well, sure, it's the kind of thing that should <i>never</i> be in the hands of any NPC, but <i>thematically</i> the <i>idea</i> of Breathing on the Black Mirror is cool, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> And now my faithfulness is rewarded. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1088967#post1088967\">Vance likes it.</a> I'm (probably) going to have an Obsidian Shards I can truly be proud of! One I won't have to constantly make excuses for!<br /> <br /> I am <i>so happy</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T19:46:16-07:00","id":1232983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1232977#post1232977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still hoping quietly for Orgiastic Fugitive to make it into Lunars. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's been brought up; Orgiastic Fugitive is being splintered into a number of intoxicant-based styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T20:03:33-07:00","id":1232984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1232983#post1232983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been brought up; Orgiastic Fugitive is being splintered into a number of intoxicant-based styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, is that so? Interesting. So quietly hoping one of them finds it's way into Lunars. Imagine, poison (drug) effects from a Toad Lunar, its perfect!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T20:04:48-07:00","id":1232986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1232983#post1232983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been brought up; Orgiastic Fugitive is being splintered into a number of intoxicant-based styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be nice for at least one of them to appear in <i>Fangs At The Gate</i>, as a wicked contrast to the ascetic, monastic martial arts traditions of the Immaculates who oppose the Lunar Exalted. The vulgar, lustful, carnal oni.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1232981#post1232981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <u>Crystal Chameleon:</u> The 3E rules for both movement and stealth might make this one tricky to implement, but &quot;disco-ninja Sonic-the-Hedgehog with a spear&quot; is such a memorable powerset. And I like Journeys having nice things. This one might be lower-priority for the devs given that White Reaper and Golden Janissary are both already available for spears in 3E, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's so much more than a &quot;spear&quot; style; in fact, little of the Style is dependent thematically upon spears. Which is why it can also be used with rope-darts.<br /> <br /> Rope-darts are another thing that don't yet have a printed Style, and Crystal Chameleon is the only one I remember from past Editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T12:43:43-07:00","id":1233069,"title":"","content":"At some point, there was mention of sorcerous martial arts. I'm afire with curiosity about what that will mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T13:43:24-07:00","id":1233077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1233069#post1233069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At some point, there was mention of sorcerous martial arts. I'm afire with curiosity about what that will mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is a sorcerous initiation focused on the martial arts in a manner sufficiently different from the asceticism of Soul-Perfecting Elixir's second ritual, and obviously using spells together with martial arts, like practicing Earth Dragon Style with Invulnerable Skin of Bronze.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T21:21:47-07:00","id":1233137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1232981#post1232981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial Arts are one of my favorite things about Exalted, and the campaign I'm currently running is MA-themed, so I am definitely all about seeing more styles.<br /> <br /> The top three I'd like to see in 3E are...<br /> <br /> - <u>Fivefold Shadow Hand Style:</u> Okay, the 2E mechanics were <i>bad</i>. Okay, it's <i>blatantly</i> trying to ape Naruto. Okay, Terrestrial styles are a hard sell for 3E when the higher-tier styles are mostly better-remembered. But. But. I just think it's fun. We can still have fun with this game, right?<br /> <br /> I also liked how all the pan-Elemental styles had different variants built in. That's good story fodder for martial artists.<br /> <br /> - <u>Crystal Chameleon:</u> The 3E rules for both movement and stealth might make this one tricky to implement, but &quot;disco-ninja Sonic-the-Hedgehog with a spear&quot; is such a memorable powerset. And I like Journeys having nice things. This one might be lower-priority for the devs given that White Reaper and Golden Janissary are both already available for spears in 3E, though.<br /> <br /> - <u>Obsidian Shards of Infinity:</u> I have spent years as a lonely defender of this style. I have spent years fending off jokes about &quot;Shattering the Balance&quot; and saying &quot;Well, sure, it's the kind of thing that should <i>never</i> be in the hands of any NPC, but <i>thematically</i> the <i>idea</i> of Breathing on the Black Mirror is cool, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> And now my faithfulness is rewarded. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1088967#post1088967\">Vance likes it.</a> I'm (probably) going to have an Obsidian Shards I can truly be proud of! One I won't have to constantly make excuses for!<br /> <br /> I am <i>so happy</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>SEVEN</b><br /> That is the number of pages it took me of meticuliously scrolling through to find one comment mentioning Obsidian Shards of Infinity. I'm quite shocked actually.<br /> <br /> I've already kinda wrote my own conversion for Grass Swaying Dance Style already, so I'm not to worried about it right now. Would love to see Monkey style again though. Hope they keep the pinnacle charm the same. I wanna swing a Grand Daiklaive by kicking with Grass Swaying.<br /> <br /> Even Blade is my third for sure. I got to play an Even-Blade practitioner once. I got to be essence 5, and the storyteller allowed me to take the first-age charm that allows me to treat my essence and melee as 1 higher for minimums to buy charms. I was a monster.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for sorcery...I've never really got to play a detailed sorcerer, so I'm really at a lost for a majority of the spells. necromancy would be nice to have back, though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12184-lazzerusthanatos","name":"LazzerusThanatos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12184_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T00:44:47-07:00","id":1233151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1232970#post1232970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not quite what irony is.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are three distinct forms of irony bandied about in literary circles. Verbal, Situational, and Dramatic. Situational irony comes into play when a scenario proceeds in a manner opposite of that which was expected. In this scenario, it was reasonable to expect that a style which had (to this point) shared the same associations with each Edition's Dragon-Blooded book that Snake Style has had with the core book would continue its service and receive a third edition update. Instead, it was omitted, and two styles that in previous editions had been very deliberately NOT associated with the Dragon-Blooded (Golden Janissary and Mantis) have taken its place. In previous editions, pretty much ALL of the zodiac styles have been things that the Realm Dragon-Blooded have been... wary... of (due to their historical association with the Anathema) while Golden Janissary had certain associations with 'encouraging mortals to act beyond their station as Champions' in Immaculate circles. Not hard and fast rules, but expectations that were previously presented as reasonable that have now been reversed. Situationally ironic, and conveying a strong message. <br /> <br /> I don't disagree with that message. Given the way Martial Arts have been restructured (doing away with the division between Terrestrial, Celestial, and Sidereal circles), opening the Immaculate Styles more broadly, and actively working to disassociate the former celestial-level zodiac styles from the Celestial Exalted who previously had something of a monopoly upon them is entirely reasonable. It's a break in a pattern that does away with a niche that used to exist, and I like it. I'll miss my 'standard issue legionnaire's martial art', but under the new writing there's no theme it speaks to that Terrestrial Brawl and/or the Immaculate Dragon styles don't serve equally well. <br /> <br /> So, yes, ironic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T03:57:21-07:00","id":1233164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1232981#post1232981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <u>Obsidian Shards of Infinity:</u> I have spent years as a lonely defender of this style. I have spent years fending off jokes about &quot;Shattering the Balance&quot; and saying &quot;Well, sure, it's the kind of thing that should <i>never</i> be in the hands of any NPC, but <i>thematically</i> the <i>idea</i> of Breathing on the Black Mirror is cool, right?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>FYI, somebody already made their own 3E version of it. <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-930#post-5975538\" target=\"_blank\">Should help to tide you over until the Sid book drops.</a><br /> <br /> (Technically, Where Fate Has Led also has its own version, but this one is vastly cooler.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T04:19:04-07:00","id":1233166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1233151#post1233151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't disagree with that message. Given the way Martial Arts have been restructured (doing away with the division between Terrestrial, Celestial, and Sidereal circles), opening the Immaculate Styles more broadly, and actively working to disassociate the former celestial-level zodiac styles from the Celestial Exalted who previously had something of a monopoly upon them is entirely reasonable. It's a break in a pattern that does away with a niche that used to exist, and I like it. I'll miss my 'standard issue legionnaire's martial art', but under the new writing there's no theme it speaks to that Terrestrial Brawl and/or the Immaculate Dragon styles don't serve equally well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The division still exists though. The terrestrial keyword weakens a lot of styles. That keyword shows quite a difference between terriestrials and celestials. Sidereal martial arts are also in another division. Last time I checked Zodiac Styles could be learned by the immaculate order. They just weren't taught because DB's had a much harder time learning CMA so it was ignored in favor of the immaculate styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 07-08-2018, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T04:50:14-07:00","id":1233168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1233166#post1233166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The division still exists though. The terrestrial keyword weakens a lot of styles. That keyword shows quite a difference between terriestrials and celestials. Sidereal martial arts are also in another division. Last time I checked Zodiac Styles could be learned by the immaculate order. They just weren't taught because DB's had a much harder time learning CMA so it was ignored in favor of the immaculate styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>The division exists in the sense that Celestials get more payout from buying Martial Arts than Terrestrials do. The process of individual martial arts being substantively weaker because they belong to a 'lesser circle' of martial art, however, is old bias. Terrestrials no longer need Initiation charms to be able to learn the Immaculate Dragon styles, because 'terrestrial martial arts' and 'celestial martial arts' are no longer categorical distinctions. This means that if you want to build a Stock DB who didn't get any training at the Cloister of Wisdom... but whose backstory involved him studying under a secular martial arts master (at home or abroad), it's entirely reasonable for him to be a Snake or Tiger stylist. The powerdown is baked into the charms, not into the style categories.<br /> <br /> It also means that Golden Janissary gets to move into the Immaculate Order's wheelhouse as a favorite tool of Immaculate exorcists, effectively helping to fill part of the niche that the initiation charms left. (I don't recall off the top of my head, but I'm pretty sure occult charms also fill in that gap.)<br /> <br /> Thinking on it, this actually opens up some interesting mental space for former Terrestrial Martial Arts with cool themes, but little-to-no love from thematically appropriate Celestial characters. <br /> <br /> A Falling Blossom stylist who falls in love with the family of aristocrats he's been tasked to protect, who ultimately Exalts as a Steward when an invasion puts them at risk, for instance. <br /> <br /> A Zenith might find themselves taken in and trained by the Just and Truthful Arbiters of Light. <br /> <br /> A Chosen of Battles, having become thoroughly weary of distractions who get in her way over the course of her assignments might take up First Pulse style to halt arguments against her recklessness from unknowing associates not cued in about her nature before they can take up much of her time. <br /> <br /> Before this paradigm adjustment, the game system actively discouraged these explorations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11867,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","user":"Caffeine Delusions","date":". 07-08-2018, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T05:55:00-07:00","id":1233177,"title":"","content":"Is there still a place for Falling Blossom in a game that no longer allows mortals to learn Martial Arts Charms, that ditched Martyr effects on Dragon-Blooded Charms to encourage us to suppose they might both survive and win battles, that includes Integrity Charms to resist fear in battle, that includes the Defend Other action from the start with excellent supporting Melee and Crane Style Charms, that gave us a much-improved version of Virtuous Negation Defense, and that will definitely include improved versions of the Lunar Charms which can be applied to parry- and evasion-based expressions of Defend Other?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T06:12:17-07:00","id":1233181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1233168#post1233168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The division exists in the sense that Celestials get more payout from buying Martial Arts than Terrestrials do. The process of individual martial arts being substantively weaker because they belong to a 'lesser circle' of martial art, however, is old bias. Terrestrials no longer need Initiation charms to be able to learn the Immaculate Dragon styles, because 'terrestrial martial arts' and 'celestial martial arts' are no longer categorical distinctions. This means that if you want to build a Stock DB who didn't get any training at the Cloister of Wisdom... but whose backstory involved him studying under a secular martial arts master (at home or abroad), it's entirely reasonable for him to be a Snake or Tiger stylist. The powerdown is baked into the charms, not into the style categories..</div> </div> </div> </div>Except this doesn't exactly change the fact that you'd get more out of the immaculate styles than you would snake or tiger. The powerdown makes it discouraging by design though. Even moreso than before because now the immaculate styles are the only way for a DB to be a better martial arts. It used to be that, you could at least learn a celestial uncap ability as a dragon blooded and then learn any Celestial martial art. It was better to learn immaculate styles by default. Now you kind of have to just deal with it and find someone who can teach you the immaculate styles. I mean sure it's shifted a bit but the distinctions still exist in a different manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T11:45:30-07:00","id":1233234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1233177#post1233177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there still a place for Falling Blossom in a game that no longer allows mortals to learn Martial Arts Charms, that ditched Martyr effects on Dragon-Blooded Charms to encourage us to suppose they might both survive and win battles, that includes Integrity Charms to resist fear in battle, that includes the Defend Other action from the start with excellent supporting Melee and Crane Style Charms, that gave us a much-improved version of Virtuous Negation Defense, and that will definitely include improved versions of the Lunar Charms which can be applied to parry- and evasion-based expressions of Defend Other?</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be done.<br /> The only charm in the style that's really about not expecting to survive the battle is Verse of the Martyr and there's fun to be had with playing someone so fanatical, I'd personally put it in Abyssals and link it to Ancestor Cults and the Shining Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T13:02:12-07:00","id":1233252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1233234#post1233234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be done.<br /> <br /> The only charm in the style that's really about not expecting to survive the battle is Verse of the Martyr and there's fun to be had with playing someone so fanatical, I'd personally put it in Abyssals and link it to Ancestor Cults and the Shining Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have an idea for what the Style looks like?<br /> <br /> In Second Edition, it used bare-handed attacks, knives, and swords. But what <i>kind </i>of bare-handed attacks, what <i>kind </i>of swords, and should it allow other sorts of weapons? Why <i>swords</i>, specifically, out of any other weapons?<br /> <br /> Should it still be incompatible with all armor? Living Shield Technique could be used with Defend Other and parrying, which is unaffected by mobility penalties, and having heavy armor would make you a more effective bodyguard.<br /> <br /> The Style is definitely going to need new Charms, and I think one that uses the martyr's shed blood to form a shield for their ward would be a cool idea. Another Charm might empower the bodyguard's weapon in proportion to the blood shed by the ward. A pinnacle Charm might instantly and completely heal the ward in return for incapacitating the martial artist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T13:51:20-07:00","id":1233258,"title":"","content":"The main thing I think a good bodyguard style needs in Ex3 is a 'Hold the Line' charm that helps your friends Disengage.<br /> <br /> As for the effects I have two main ideas.<br /> -It should also encourage you to build a strong relationship with a dedicated Ward in a manner similar to the old conviction virtue. Distinguishing it from Crane Style.<br /> -There should be optional health level costs throughout the style to keep the theme of martyrdom alive even if your character doesn't sacrifice themselves during the game.<br /> <br /> Form weapons and armour I'm unsure on right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T14:19:52-07:00","id":1233264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1233181#post1233181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except this doesn't exactly change the fact that you'd get more out of the immaculate styles than you would snake or tiger. The powerdown makes it discouraging by design though. Even moreso than before because now the immaculate styles are the only way for a DB to be a better martial arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguable. Conversely, there are now a whole bunch of styles that'd been mechanically and narratively gated off away from Terrestrials that they can now learn, even if they get less utility out of them than a more powerful exalt type would. Being a better martial artist isn't always a matter of using one style well; it can also be a matter of being conversant in multiple styles, each of which has a distinct utility, and which synergize to make the martial artist using them a more challenging combatant. The 'Style Generalist' who moves smoothly from Snake to Crane to Mantis is at least as firmly entrenched a trope as the style specialist who masters Earth Dragon Style and makes that the end of his exploration. <br /> <br /> Granted, I will say that the way the Immaculate styles really depend on interacting with the new Elemental Aura mechanic really drives a knife through the heart of one of my old stock characters (a Zenith caste ne'er-do-well drunk who happened to be trained in Fire Dragon Style)... but I'm willing to pay that price for the styles to have niche protection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T14:28:40-07:00","id":1233270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1233258#post1233258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Form weapons and armour I'm unsure on right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like where your head's at. Sunder's doing some good thinking as well, there. I think the biggest utility with knives in the context of a bodyguard style is that they're the kind of weapon that a noncombatant protectee would be most likely to toss a bodyguard who for one reason or other might be otherwise unarmed. If a state dinner requires that bodyguards give up their swords, a style that incorporates knife training can re-arm the guard with steak knives. In a lot of cultures, a knife or dagger is considered an 'everyday carry' item used for utility more often than combat, and their ubiquity makes them a good choice for a style that stresses vigilance. <br /> <br /> Sword... My perception is that it fills the traditional role of the 'standard sidearm' in this scenario. A sword makes a statement about combat readiness without necessarily making a like statement about eagerness. The fact that it's also the weapon most commonly paired with a shield makes a statement in itself, and Sunder makes a good case for making 'sword and board' the most distinctive signature for a rebuild of the style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T14:50:32-07:00","id":1233280,"title":"","content":"Axes are more common than swords, being cheaper and easier to make, as well as tools that most people in the world won\u2019t give a second glance. Think about how many axes you see behind the words Break Glass In Case Of Emergency, and then remember that fire was a more frequent hazard when everything is made of wood.<br /> <br /> I always thought daggers were a good choice for the reasons you laid out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T17:19:35-07:00","id":1233313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1233264#post1233264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arguable. Conversely, there are now a whole bunch of styles that'd been mechanically and narratively gated off away from Terrestrials that they can now learn, even if they get less utility out of them than a more powerful exalt type would. Being a better martial artist isn't always a matter of using one style well; it can also be a matter of being conversant in multiple styles, each of which has a distinct utility, and which synergize to make the martial artist using them a more challenging combatant. The 'Style Generalist' who moves smoothly from Snake to Crane to Mantis is at least as firmly entrenched a trope as the style specialist who masters Earth Dragon Style and makes that the end of his exploration. <br /> <br /> Granted, I will say that the way the Immaculate styles really depend on interacting with the new Elemental Aura mechanic really drives a knife through the heart of one of my old stock characters (a Zenith caste ne'er-do-well drunk who happened to be trained in Fire Dragon Style)... but I'm willing to pay that price for the styles to have niche protection.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's objectively inferior now. An immaculate style pactitioner gets to use his aura to remove all terrestrial keywords, in his form for a tick. Just knowing any of the immaculate styles makes you a head above other dragonblooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T17:39:16-07:00","id":1233315,"title":"","content":"Epimethius, I'm unclear as to your argument. I didn't claim that the Martial Arts restructuring did or was intended to put Terrestrials on the same mechanical level as other Exalt types. My point was that at this point, the new structure gives a broader range of options to EVERY martial artist. <br /> <br /> As for Immaculate styles putting one Dragon-Blooded a cut above his peers... they did in previous editions as well, and required a greater investment for it. At this point, I'd argue that is classified as a feature, not a bug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T18:45:37-07:00","id":1233319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1233315#post1233315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Epimethius, I'm unclear as to your argument. I didn't claim that the Martial Arts restructuring did or was intended to put Terrestrials on the same mechanical level as other Exalt types. My point was that at this point, the new structure gives a broader range of options to EVERY martial artist.<br /> <br /> As for Immaculate styles putting one Dragon-Blooded a cut above his peers... they did in previous editions as well, and required a greater investment for it. At this point, I'd argue that is classified as a feature, not a bug.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose my point is that the circles still exist. They're just mechanically different. SMA is still it's own thing with the same restrictions as the previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T19:03:40-07:00","id":1233324,"title":"","content":"Didn't Holden once write a Style designed by and for Lunar Exalted, called Blood Dancer Style or something similar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T21:27:00-07:00","id":1233336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1233319#post1233319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose my point is that the circles still exist. They're just mechanically different. SMA is still it's own thing with the same restrictions as the previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ish. The power differential still exists... and should, honestly. There needed to be a way to functionally represent the ways in which Terrestrial level, Celestial level, and Solar level practitioners were able to get different power outputs from their martial arts styles... but I'm still kind of celebrating the fact that it's now no longer narratively and mechanically arduous for a Terrestrial to take up something like Dreaming Pearl Courtesan style, or Tiger Style, and no longer inherently sub-par for a Lunar or Solar to pick up something like White Veil Style, or Golden Janissary style. Decoupling the power differential from distinct groupings of styles was a good move. <br /> <br /> It also allows for the distinction between regular martial arts and Sidereal martial arts to take on a different tone. Rather than being the top tier of an ascent that some players may want to rush to, if able, the comparison I could most aptly draw is between external martial arts focused on perfecting the body (Kung Fu being the classic example), and internal martial arts focused on perfecting the spirit or soul (Qigong, for instance, at least based upon the claims it makes). It taps into the notion that the external styles are things you learn in order to prepare yourself for the internal styles, and that someone reaching for the power of a Sidereal martial art before they're ready for it may actually do themselves more harm than good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T21:58:19-07:00","id":1233608,"title":"","content":"Not to derail the current conversations, but Hungry Ghost has always been one of my favorites. I am interested in seeing its mote manipulation charms in 3ed. I am a little surprised it hasn't been mentioned more.<br /> <br /> I was always a fan of monkey. 2ed monkey style was very dissapointing.<br /> <br /> After that, I think any of the former terrestrial styles would be nice to see be implemented in 3ed.<br /> <br /> I was never really into sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1767-thousand-forged-lurker","name":"Thousand forged lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T01:04:04-07:00","id":1233639,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd like to see Monkey style as it's one of the five animal styles, but I don't think it needs to be anything much like 2nd ed Monkey style.<br /> <br /> I liked Hungry Ghost too, thematically, though it was a bit mechanically random.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T02:47:35-07:00","id":1233643,"title":"","content":"I would love to see Crimson Pentacle Blade Style, Even Blade Style, and any kind of sorcerous martial arts style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T05:52:37-07:00","id":1233667,"title":"","content":"Personally I'm waiting for Hungry Ghost Style (and Abyssals at all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T06:03:48-07:00","id":1233964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1233639#post1233639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked Hungry Ghost too, thematically, though it was a bit mechanically random.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hungry Ghost definitely needs some tidying done if we're going to reintroduce it. Manipulating how folks get to spend their Essence needs to be handled with care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-11-2018, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T06:16:35-07:00","id":1233969,"title":"","content":"Wasn\u2019t it also pretty damn big for a non-Sidereal Martial Art?<br /> <br /> With the Abyssals emulating ghosts more than painting Solar Charms black, maybe a few of HGS\u2019s Charms could become native for Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T07:09:57-07:00","id":1233988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814854-top-3-martial-arts-styles-and-spell-you-are-waiting-for?p=1233964#post1233964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hungry Ghost definitely needs some tidying done if we're going to reintroduce it. Manipulating how folks get to spend their Essence needs to be handled with care.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I didn't see a great need for that kind of charm in a style about emulating hungry ghosts. And as Sunder pointed out, it was huge; not everything needs to be kept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T07:46:19-07:00","id":1233995,"title":"","content":"Hungry Ghost is <i>weird</i>. It's like parts of it were written by someone who wasn't entirely sure what one was and made a lot of assumptions about them being unpleasant ghosts based on the name, it'd be like if Tiger Style had charms that referenced having an intimidating mane and hunting in prides because... fuck it, a Lion is similar enough, right?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T15:50:05-07:00","id":1234104,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have a record of Holden\u2019s Elegant Blood-Dancer Style? I can\u2019t seem to find a copy on the internet. The old resource website is dead, and none of the newer ones have it.<br /> <br /> Edit: Found it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-11-2018, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T14:50:53-07:00","id":1234791,"title":"","content":"I don't have first ed in front of me, but I recall thinking how different 2ed Hungry Ghost was from 1ed when I first read it. Both the type of charms and the amount. I need to dig up my old 1ed Abyssals book and compare. But it has always been one of my favorites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1767-thousand-forged-lurker","name":"Thousand forged lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}